WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:06.720
Robo Warrior, your Zed, half man, half cyborg, the one man battalion with a human heart and

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:07.980
a computer's brain.

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:30.520
And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:32.440
I'm Mike. I'm Sean.

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:34.820
I'm Joe. And I'm Sam.

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:36.900
What is up everybody?

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:39.740
I'm not going to even let you answer that question.

00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:41.100
I'm going to get right to the facts.

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:45.180
We are playing a Bomberman game, whether you like it or know it or not.

00:00:45.340 --> 00:00:47.260
It is true. This is a Bomberman game.

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:51.840
Like it just feels like Bomberman or it literally is Bomberman?

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:58.620
In Japan, this game was called Bomber King and Bomberman came out in Japan in 1985.

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:02.900
So it's weird that we're actually getting this game before we get Bomberman proper.

00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:07.300
But I know that like just because Bomber's in the name doesn't confirm anything.

00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:09.820
But they're also both made by Hudson Soft.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:17.300
And in Japan, they use the same art for this Robo Warrior guy as they do for Bomberman.

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:22.320
So therefore, Robo Warrior is Bomberman and is considered part of that universe.

00:01:22.580 --> 00:01:28.320
So is the plot of Bomberman like in some way connected to this?

00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:29.760
I have no idea.

00:01:30.140 --> 00:01:31.400
I don't think Zed.

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:34.880
I don't think Zed has ever been name dropped in Bomberman games.

00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:36.960
But Zed's dead, baby.

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:38.960
Zed's dead. Zed.

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:41.660
That's a Pulp Fiction reference, guys.

00:01:41.660 --> 00:01:42.580
Yeah, I knew I recognized that. Yeah, okay.

00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:44.720
It's like a lot of silence.

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:45.820
A lot of silence there.

00:01:46.280 --> 00:01:47.940
We just wanted Olivia to try that.

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:53.900
Yeah. I don't want the viewers to think we're so young that we don't know what Pulp Fiction is.

00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:56.560
Pulp Fiction was one of those old movies.

00:01:57.500 --> 00:01:58.640
Inverse of Joe's question.

00:01:58.860 --> 00:02:01.460
In Japan, is it the same story?

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:03.180
Is this game the same story?

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:04.520
Do you know? Oh, yeah.

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:05.540
That's a good question.

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:07.980
Unlike Joe's stupid question.

00:02:09.240 --> 00:02:10.540
Isn't it the same question?

00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:12.020
No. No, no, no.

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:13.660
Because in Japan, I get it.

00:02:13.780 --> 00:02:19.740
Yeah. In Japan, it would be possibly a different story that would connect it to the Bomberman universe.

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:23.640
Whereas here, they're clearly not trying to make any connection to Bomberman.

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:29.120
True. Yeah. I mean, I don't know if you guys read the story in the manual about what the heck is going

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:30.780
on with this game, but...

00:02:30.780 --> 00:02:31.740
I'm on chapter six.

00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:33.160
It's kind of wild.

00:02:33.320 --> 00:02:36.760
Yeah. You want to run us through it?

00:02:37.700 --> 00:02:41.820
It's a lot of exposition for a game that I don't think really needs it.

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:44.220
Like, they give you a backstory to the backstory.

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:47.480
It's funny, though, because for having so much information, I feel like it just kind of

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:49.360
starts in the... It's like the Star Wars original.

00:02:49.540 --> 00:02:51.140
It just starts in the middle of the story.

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:54.620
Like, there should be a prequel now that explains what the heck they're talking about right off

00:02:54.620 --> 00:02:56.440
the bat. Yeah.

00:02:56.640 --> 00:02:58.960
Like, they talk about how the planet was named.

00:02:59.820 --> 00:03:02.280
And then that's, like, half of the description.

00:03:03.220 --> 00:03:04.780
And then it's, like, what's actually...

00:03:04.780 --> 00:03:09.320
Like, why... What's actually happening to start off the events of the game.

00:03:09.480 --> 00:03:11.800
Right. Yeah, that's not enough for me.

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:16.860
I... I need, like, the reason for, you know, like, why was the planet created?

00:03:17.080 --> 00:03:18.500
Forget the name. Like, give me the...

00:03:19.180 --> 00:03:25.240
Overpopulation. It's funny that, like, the backstory for this game, which is actually much more detailed

00:03:25.240 --> 00:03:30.060
than, like, pretty much any other manual backstory that we've read.

00:03:30.700 --> 00:03:31.780
Maybe not Scoon.

00:03:31.960 --> 00:03:33.100
It basically was overpopulation.

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:36.580
So they just created an artificial planet.

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:41.460
Never mind, like, trying to find a new one, because apparently we have...

00:03:41.460 --> 00:03:44.720
We can't find new planets, but we have the resources to create our own.

00:03:44.720 --> 00:03:52.020
Then it's, like, another millennia or so, because they've even changed the way that we name our years.

00:03:53.260 --> 00:03:54.560
And we've all...

00:03:54.560 --> 00:03:57.840
And all humans have forgotten what war even is.

00:03:58.200 --> 00:03:59.480
And then we're...

00:03:59.480 --> 00:04:00.860
The new planet is invaded.

00:04:01.100 --> 00:04:08.200
I don't know. It just seems like a really roundabout way of, like, it not being Earth that's been invaded and destroyed.

00:04:08.440 --> 00:04:11.180
Like, I feel like this could have just been Earth being invaded.

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:14.940
Right. Yeah, like, we didn't need all this, like, extra...

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:15.920
It's extra steps.

00:04:16.100 --> 00:04:17.840
It's that... No one's really in it for the story.

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:20.380
But I also thought it was funny that it starts out...

00:04:20.380 --> 00:04:21.280
Like, the first sentence is,

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:25.740
In the year 2395, Earth scientists and engineers follow a tiles...

00:04:25.740 --> 00:04:26.920
Altiles plans?

00:04:28.260 --> 00:04:29.280
What? That just...

00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:30.800
It just starts there. He's the scientist boy.

00:04:31.020 --> 00:04:34.020
Yeah. But it didn't, like, give us any...

00:04:34.020 --> 00:04:35.260
We don't know who that is yet or anything.

00:04:35.380 --> 00:04:36.760
It just says they followed his plans.

00:04:37.100 --> 00:04:41.280
I think... I'm not sure if yours is cut off, but mine starts before that.

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:42.100
Oh, okay.

00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:44.780
On the left side. I actually didn't even see this paragraph that's under the title.

00:04:44.920 --> 00:04:46.860
There's a whole other paragraph there that I just missed.

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:48.780
Back to chapter one, Joe.

00:04:49.240 --> 00:04:51.300
Okay. Now it makes more sense.

00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:57.860
Yeah. And, you know, you guys are questioning why it had to ever start with Earth or ever move

00:04:57.860 --> 00:05:01.980
away from Earth. But otherwise, we'd have no explanation for Zed's name.

00:05:02.220 --> 00:05:04.320
He is the Z-type Earth defense.

00:05:04.820 --> 00:05:06.520
But that would make sense on Earth.

00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:09.380
Yeah, more sense on Earth.

00:05:09.380 --> 00:05:11.300
That's not cool if it takes place on Earth.

00:05:11.320 --> 00:05:15.640
It has to take place on another planet, but then he is somehow, like, from Earth.

00:05:15.920 --> 00:05:16.800
It's nice. Nice.

00:05:17.500 --> 00:05:18.980
I don't agree.

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:20.820
I'm just gonna end with that.

00:05:21.720 --> 00:05:25.660
All right. Well, in this game, players play as Zed.

00:05:25.900 --> 00:05:30.660
You have to fight the Xantho Empire.

00:05:31.380 --> 00:05:33.100
Destroy its leader, Xur.

00:05:33.100 --> 00:05:36.100
And you do that by...

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:39.240
Zed uses primarily bombs, just like Bomberman.

00:05:39.680 --> 00:05:42.200
And he does that to hurt his enemies.

00:05:42.200 --> 00:05:45.300
He has a gun and a bunch of other things to destroy his surroundings.

00:05:45.840 --> 00:05:48.660
And there's various hidden items in each stage.

00:05:48.940 --> 00:05:50.860
This is my, like, generic overview of the game.

00:05:50.960 --> 00:05:54.240
But I think it'd be a lot more helpful if we just kind of...

00:05:54.240 --> 00:05:55.460
I don't know.

00:05:56.080 --> 00:06:00.840
Talked about, like, what the main objective of this game is.

00:06:00.840 --> 00:06:07.140
Because every level is kind of similar in the sense that you have to just place your bombs,

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:10.240
blow up your surroundings, uncover cool stuff,

00:06:10.460 --> 00:06:16.460
and find, like, either a key or a secret door or an exit of some sort in each level.

00:06:17.260 --> 00:06:21.240
And I wonder from, you know, maybe one at a time, Sean, we'll start with you.

00:06:21.500 --> 00:06:27.860
Is it satisfying to play this game, to bomb stuff, and to look for these hidden items?

00:06:29.720 --> 00:06:36.360
Well, yeah. Yeah, like, so we just reviewed a game that the main concept is destruction of the environment.

00:06:36.360 --> 00:06:37.480
And here's another one.

00:06:37.600 --> 00:06:38.680
It's a little bit...

00:06:39.740 --> 00:06:42.900
It's a little bit more the focus, in a way.

00:06:43.260 --> 00:06:45.580
In that any...

00:06:45.580 --> 00:06:48.680
Actually, no. They're both kind of equally about blowing stuff up.

00:06:48.780 --> 00:06:52.780
But this one's a bit more puzzle-like, and it's not as mindless.

00:06:54.420 --> 00:07:00.500
I'd say it was satisfying, just the act of laying bombs and watching it take out whatever's around.

00:07:00.920 --> 00:07:07.400
I had some issues with the design, but I'm sure I'll get into that later.

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:09.340
Yeah, I would agree with that.

00:07:09.460 --> 00:07:13.640
I think that whereas the last game we play is more about destroying the environment,

00:07:13.780 --> 00:07:17.680
this one's about finding things in a destructible environment, which I think is a little different.

00:07:17.680 --> 00:07:21.240
And I think that moving the...

00:07:21.240 --> 00:07:23.640
Like, the controls feel really good and very tight.

00:07:24.560 --> 00:07:30.560
And moving everything and shooting and placing bombs and changing your weapons out, I think that all works great.

00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:36.620
But the point of the game, I think, is a little bit lost.

00:07:37.100 --> 00:07:41.640
And it can be a bit frustrating to navigate, and we'll get into that later.

00:07:41.920 --> 00:07:43.540
So I feel like I'm on the same page.

00:07:43.780 --> 00:07:49.560
Sorry. I think if it comes down to being like, is it literally satisfying to lay the bombs and blow things up?

00:07:49.640 --> 00:07:51.240
Like, in that sense, yes.

00:07:51.500 --> 00:07:54.420
But I was left wanting more.

00:07:54.880 --> 00:07:58.660
It starts out kind of leading you to think like, okay, this is this interesting maze game.

00:07:59.300 --> 00:08:01.200
Yes, there are puzzle elements to it.

00:08:01.300 --> 00:08:04.960
But that never really becomes much of a thing.

00:08:05.220 --> 00:08:08.700
I never felt like, oh, I got to solve this interesting puzzle.

00:08:09.960 --> 00:08:15.000
It's either like, oh, yeah, just blow up as much of the environment as you can to find your way out.

00:08:15.100 --> 00:08:18.420
Just blow through forests of these trees.

00:08:18.680 --> 00:08:21.380
Like, literally just dense forests of these obstacles.

00:08:21.500 --> 00:08:22.760
Just keep blowing them up.

00:08:22.860 --> 00:08:24.340
Keep getting bombs. Keep blowing them up.

00:08:24.820 --> 00:08:28.380
Or it's like this find a secret that there's really no clues to.

00:08:28.540 --> 00:08:31.600
Or just keep blowing things up until you find the hidden item that lets you move on.

00:08:32.000 --> 00:08:37.740
We never felt like there was, like, enough of a maze element to make the bombing part, like, feel satisfying.

00:08:38.280 --> 00:08:46.300
Yeah, I think that the bombing aspect itself, right, of, like, laying down the bombs and you have to, like, get away because they're dangerous and explosion.

00:08:46.620 --> 00:08:48.760
And then, like, the explosion isn't perfect.

00:08:48.760 --> 00:08:53.000
It actually, like, for certain pixels, it'll, like, leave half a dent or something.

00:08:53.000 --> 00:08:54.520
I think that's, like, a nice touch as well.

00:08:54.660 --> 00:09:03.000
There's all the good, like, foundations of using the bombs as, like, your main attack and having that be a satisfying action to clear out what's in front of you.

00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:09.600
But there's just some small little things that I nitpick on that make it ultimately not that much fun.

00:09:09.720 --> 00:09:11.020
It pushes in the other direction.

00:09:11.440 --> 00:09:19.160
First thing I'm going to mention is just for all of these levels, keep in mind, like, this is a top-down, like, Zelda-looking style game.

00:09:19.660 --> 00:09:24.440
And if you think about the bombs that you can get in a Zelda game, it's the same thing here.

00:09:24.580 --> 00:09:27.140
You lay them out and they explode and they reveal passages.

00:09:27.140 --> 00:09:28.040
It's very similar.

00:09:28.680 --> 00:09:33.280
Here, whenever you lay down a bomb, which, remember, is something that you do all the time,

00:09:33.440 --> 00:09:39.240
whenever you lay one down, you get this weird, like, pushback or bounce away from the bomb.

00:09:42.460 --> 00:09:44.780
Mm-hmm.

00:10:09.240 --> 00:10:15.340
What Joe was saying about, like, if there was an actual puzzle exploration element to it and a more purposeful bombing,

00:10:15.780 --> 00:10:21.500
it could have been more fun than just, well, to always move forward, you always have to bomb.

00:10:22.900 --> 00:10:30.540
Yeah. So I found out several times that I seem to have been playing this game wrong.

00:10:32.140 --> 00:10:41.000
I'd say that I do appreciate that the very beginning of the game sort of is just a free-form tutorial.

00:10:41.420 --> 00:10:46.500
Like, they give you a bunch of pickups that sort of, like, tells you what these pickups do.

00:10:46.940 --> 00:10:52.740
They give you some stuff to bomb, but it's not like this isn't the game proper yet.

00:10:52.740 --> 00:10:56.180
I appreciate that kind of, like, teaching moment.

00:10:56.860 --> 00:11:01.160
But that just sort of tells you how to control the game mechanically.

00:11:01.160 --> 00:11:03.900
It's not really telling you how you should play.

00:11:06.520 --> 00:11:11.780
So I was sort of just trying to find the path of least resistance because throughout this game,

00:11:12.860 --> 00:11:21.060
you see that there's, like, rock formations that are sort of, like, the base, like, those you can't blow through.

00:11:21.220 --> 00:11:22.840
It's really just blow up the trees.

00:11:22.840 --> 00:11:32.640
And those will expose some pickups and move your way through this, like, mini maze.

00:11:34.280 --> 00:11:41.340
But it turns out that you pretty much have to just clear whatever you can.

00:11:41.520 --> 00:11:45.640
Like, it may not be the way you need to go, but you should probably blow up everything.

00:11:45.640 --> 00:11:51.240
Not just so that you have more space to move around and not get blown up by your own bombs,

00:11:51.280 --> 00:11:55.920
but because to find some of the items that you need to pick up to progress,

00:11:55.980 --> 00:11:59.980
they may be hidden in, like, this out-of-the-way part of the forest.

00:12:00.160 --> 00:12:05.100
Like, I don't know if I'm rambling right now, but I felt that, like,

00:12:06.220 --> 00:12:12.560
what I was doing was, like, trying to find the way to use the least amount of bombs to get through this level.

00:12:13.160 --> 00:12:15.760
But you should be spamming this shit.

00:12:15.980 --> 00:12:17.320
It's completely...

00:12:17.320 --> 00:12:20.700
It was completely unintuitive for me.

00:12:21.020 --> 00:12:22.840
I don't know what your guys' experience was.

00:12:23.180 --> 00:12:26.580
Well, I think that just, like, brings it back to, like, it's not really a puzzle,

00:12:26.700 --> 00:12:28.800
where it feels like it's just finding a needle in a haystack.

00:12:28.940 --> 00:12:31.120
It's just look everywhere until you find it.

00:12:32.200 --> 00:12:40.540
Which, I mean, as you can imagine, gets kind of old after it just screams and screams full of the same thing.

00:12:40.540 --> 00:12:42.560
And, you know, there's more to it than that.

00:12:42.640 --> 00:12:45.840
But just on that level, like, that's kind of how it feels.

00:12:46.700 --> 00:12:54.160
Yeah. And I ran into this problem also, so I looked up, you know, what people...

00:12:54.160 --> 00:12:59.900
I looked up a speedrun of the game, and in the first area, or the second area where you can go,

00:13:00.320 --> 00:13:03.600
there's a little hidden staircase to get to the underground.

00:13:04.140 --> 00:13:05.740
So if you have a candle in the underground...

00:13:05.740 --> 00:13:10.080
But, you know, no one's going to know that it's there unless you bomb a very specific area.

00:13:10.760 --> 00:13:17.040
Um, and then when you're in the underground, it kind of acts as, like, a hub where you can pick up all sorts of things really easily,

00:13:17.040 --> 00:13:19.960
because there's no trees and no obstacles to bomb except for enemies.

00:13:20.420 --> 00:13:21.320
That kind of...

00:13:21.320 --> 00:13:25.840
I can kind of see how that, like, fits into the loop a little bit.

00:13:26.800 --> 00:13:30.920
But even then, when I was in there, I had a candle that you're supposed to use to light it up.

00:13:30.920 --> 00:13:37.860
And then after a while, the candle went out, and I didn't know where the exit was, because I didn't have a candle, and there were no lights.

00:13:38.240 --> 00:13:50.840
I was just going to say, that same thing happened to me, and just a little behind the scenes here as to, like, what I've been thinking lately is that there's been a few games lately that we played that I feel kind of bad that I've...

00:13:51.380 --> 00:13:57.720
After the first level, recently, I've been like, okay, I'll just look up a walkthrough, or I'll look up a playthrough.

00:13:57.900 --> 00:14:04.900
And I was like, said to myself, I'm not going to do that this time, or I'm at least going to make some significant progress, because I feel like there's been a few in the last couple of episodes.

00:14:06.760 --> 00:14:13.680
So, first of all, I spent, like, 40 minutes on that first level, trying to figure out how to stop it from looping, because it loops.

00:14:13.680 --> 00:14:17.340
Yeah, so was I. And there's, like, a hidden chalice somewhere.

00:14:17.560 --> 00:14:21.880
Then I thought I had found a way out by going down into that basement area.

00:14:22.440 --> 00:14:24.940
Went down there, I had two candles, I used them both.

00:14:25.320 --> 00:14:31.660
Then, only after they were gone, I realized that the only way out is the way in, which I couldn't remember exactly where it was.

00:14:31.660 --> 00:14:35.240
And if you can't remember exactly where it was, you're just walking in the dark with no clue.

00:14:35.720 --> 00:14:39.200
Walked around there for another 20 minutes before I was just like, I'm just going to start over.

00:14:39.640 --> 00:14:42.620
This game took me so long to play, and I still didn't get that far in it.

00:14:43.420 --> 00:14:50.020
Yeah, when you get down there, and you've run out of candle, because, again, that's the only way that you can see.

00:14:50.160 --> 00:14:53.960
It gives you, like, a 5x5 grid of light.

00:14:53.960 --> 00:15:05.120
If you run out of candle, it's not like a soft lock, because if you just keep, like, scanning, eventually you'll come across the stairwell again.

00:15:05.420 --> 00:15:09.160
But it may as well be, because that would be such a tedious task.

00:15:10.980 --> 00:15:15.360
So it's sort of the same as that, like, endless loop unless you find the chalice.

00:15:16.320 --> 00:15:23.320
It seems like the kind of game that you would, like, grind in the 80s with, you know?

00:15:23.940 --> 00:15:29.120
Like, if you had nothing to do, you'd just be like, alright, I finally figured out that that's where the staircase is.

00:15:29.260 --> 00:15:32.920
And so that's just cemented in my 8-year-old memory now.

00:15:33.180 --> 00:15:35.780
And so I'm always going to remember that the staircase is right there.

00:15:36.320 --> 00:15:44.860
And I'm going to go back and, you know, use that information to get into the underground and then back up.

00:15:45.580 --> 00:15:48.500
And, you know, so you, like, kind of...

00:15:48.500 --> 00:15:52.360
It seems like the kind of thing that you gain more...

00:15:52.980 --> 00:15:57.480
Skill isn't the right word, but just experience with the more you do it.

00:15:57.540 --> 00:16:05.440
And that lets you have more fun with it, just because you know the ins and outs of this kind of nonsensical level layout.

00:16:05.800 --> 00:16:12.100
Well, I think it's really for fans of, like, you know, the Legend of Zelda-style exploration of an overworld,

00:16:12.260 --> 00:16:14.200
where you're, like, just looking for something.

00:16:14.200 --> 00:16:18.500
You know, I think the most appropriate example is the, you know, Needle in the Haystack,

00:16:18.620 --> 00:16:20.440
where it's like, you're looking for that one particular thing,

00:16:20.580 --> 00:16:23.300
but at least you're rewarded with other things along the way.

00:16:23.460 --> 00:16:28.540
There's, like, a possible chance to run into a shop or to get a cool power-up.

00:16:28.540 --> 00:16:38.980
And the power-ups are great because they'll actually, like, help you, for the most part, clear out or navigate the level in a way that the bombs are just a very frustrating experience.

00:16:39.100 --> 00:16:45.740
After the, like, even after the 20th bomb you lay down, you're like, oh, this is the game, huh?

00:16:46.200 --> 00:16:48.200
Like, this is the loop, like, this is what happens?

00:16:48.940 --> 00:16:53.240
I was thinking about comparing this to Zelda, or I was comparing it to Zelda, I guess.

00:16:54.540 --> 00:17:01.860
As I was playing it, because I know that there's some trees in Zelda you have to burn down and things like that to get secret spots.

00:17:03.380 --> 00:17:08.060
But Zelda isn't a linear game that requires you to go from point A to point B.

00:17:08.360 --> 00:17:12.900
Like, you eventually have to go beat Ganon, you know, but how you go about that, it's kind of up to you.

00:17:13.220 --> 00:17:18.060
Whereas in this, you really just need to get to the end of each level.

00:17:18.360 --> 00:17:21.920
And so I don't know if that works quite as well.

00:17:22.960 --> 00:17:32.180
Well, one thing that I noticed that was, like, okay, so I learned my lesson, so I went and watched a similar video.

00:17:32.280 --> 00:17:35.060
I don't think it was a speed run, but it was, like, a long play of the game.

00:17:35.080 --> 00:17:41.220
And I noticed the huge difference in play style between what I was doing and what this player was doing.

00:17:41.220 --> 00:17:55.600
And once I started to emulate that and stopped trying to, like, just, like, do as little as I can, play more conservatively, I just started to, like, you know, spam the bombs pretty much on every tree that I saw.

00:17:55.720 --> 00:18:00.700
And once you get into that groove, like, you don't end up in a situation where, like, oh, I'm out of bombs.

00:18:00.700 --> 00:18:08.080
I have to wait for these, like, trash mobs to sort of come into my area so that I can use two more bombs and get stuck again.

00:18:08.080 --> 00:18:15.620
Then you start to, like, you get to more of a flow because now you have a better inventory to work with.

00:18:16.680 --> 00:18:21.300
Because you're blowing so much stuff up, you get a lot more power-ups.

00:18:21.420 --> 00:18:25.680
So you get a little bit more creativity in how you get to a protein situation.

00:18:26.460 --> 00:18:37.080
So I would have really appreciated that being more natural, like, coming across this play style would be more natural.

00:18:37.080 --> 00:18:43.120
But once I was told to play that way, I enjoyed this game much more.

00:18:43.900 --> 00:18:46.120
And here's why it's not natural, though, Sean.

00:18:46.280 --> 00:18:53.640
I think it has a lot to do with the immediate understanding, you know, maybe, like, a minute into your playthrough where you realize,

00:18:53.800 --> 00:18:59.200
well, I'm cleaning house, like, I'm not getting hit by my own bombs, I'm not being attacked by enemies.

00:18:59.200 --> 00:19:01.180
But what the heck's going on with my health?

00:19:01.520 --> 00:19:05.040
And then you read up on the manual and you're like, oh, I run on batteries.

00:19:05.920 --> 00:19:06.720
And so...

00:19:06.720 --> 00:19:10.560
Well, that was another thing. Like, just I always get a constant power drain.

00:19:10.720 --> 00:19:16.260
And so I think that's why you took the, like, path of, you know, technically most resistance.

00:19:16.600 --> 00:19:20.120
Yeah, exactly. So I was trying to go as, like, just get to the end.

00:19:20.120 --> 00:19:25.780
And it told me in the manual that there would be some levels that you needed this thing or else it would keep looping.

00:19:25.900 --> 00:19:27.760
I did not know it was going to be the first level.

00:19:27.900 --> 00:19:37.780
But I also didn't know that, like, when you get those power-ups that refill your batteries, I didn't know that you had to actively use them.

00:19:38.420 --> 00:19:44.420
So I'm playing the game for, like, a few minutes and I just keep dying because I'm just running out of batteries immediately.

00:19:44.720 --> 00:19:50.560
Little do I know that I have an inventory filled with, like, three or four of these things that refill you to max health.

00:19:51.660 --> 00:19:55.860
And so just learning that took a good 15 to 20 minutes.

00:19:56.240 --> 00:19:59.500
And that was not even with me changing the way I played the game.

00:19:59.580 --> 00:20:01.880
That was just learning how the inventory worked.

00:20:02.560 --> 00:20:08.560
Right, right. Ultimately, it's, like, it's a clever explanation for, like, a robot that runs on batteries, right?

00:20:08.800 --> 00:20:16.380
But it kind of, it limits the fun of the game as you have to, like, manage your health as a constant thing.

00:20:16.740 --> 00:20:27.280
Imagine if, you know, since we're talking about Legend of Zelda, like, imagine if Link constantly required you to go into the menu and use the Triforce of Courage or whatever he has.

00:20:27.420 --> 00:20:33.880
I think it's Courage. And you had to constantly click on that to, like, replenish your health because otherwise he was constantly losing.

00:20:34.600 --> 00:20:41.580
Because, you know, going back to the fact that you have to lay down these bombs all the time, you lay down the bomb, you get that pushback I talked about earlier.

00:20:41.620 --> 00:20:46.280
You got to make sure you don't get hit by these things because the bombs do an incredible amount of damage.

00:20:46.280 --> 00:20:51.140
And you're already draining down damage as you're going, so you can't afford to.

00:20:51.380 --> 00:21:03.080
So you're almost, like, the whole game, you're playing this game of, like, drop the bomb and run, but also do something else because you're going to have to maintain this power drain that's going on.

00:21:03.080 --> 00:21:08.340
And you're going to want to lay down bombs in other places as well to pick up things more frequently.

00:21:08.780 --> 00:21:16.960
However, because of the tight passageways, there's not really an opportunity for that because you'll get hit by one or the other in your...

00:21:16.960 --> 00:21:18.540
Well, that's the thing, Mike.

00:21:18.800 --> 00:21:23.720
You got to keep, like, that's sort of that playstyle, that faster, more loose playstyle.

00:21:23.720 --> 00:21:26.920
You just keep bombing to widen those passageways.

00:21:27.080 --> 00:21:33.280
So as you're going, it's sort of like you're making a wide mine in Minecraft in a way.

00:21:33.360 --> 00:21:43.720
I don't know. It's just like you just keep going and it becomes a lot easier to deal with the, I guess, shrapnel from these bombs.

00:21:44.860 --> 00:21:49.060
And it was just like a flip was switched when I figured that out.

00:21:49.060 --> 00:21:56.100
And I didn't really mind that, like, very quick recovery time that you had to just get away from the bomb.

00:21:57.040 --> 00:22:01.180
But again, it's just, like, not clear that that's the way you're supposed to play the game.

00:22:01.740 --> 00:22:04.020
Right. Well, as far as, like, the...

00:22:04.020 --> 00:22:12.120
I don't know. As far as what you were talking about with the, I don't know, I guess it's sort of a time limit, the health kind of diminishing.

00:22:13.060 --> 00:22:16.780
I feel like we talk about this in other games a lot and it's always been my opinion.

00:22:16.780 --> 00:22:23.160
I think it's always... I think we've always all kind of agreed that, like, it's never really fit in the game that we played.

00:22:23.460 --> 00:22:28.800
So in this case, I mean, I think it's the same opinion for me.

00:22:28.920 --> 00:22:35.940
I do feel like that gameplay mechanic is not inherently a bad gameplay mechanic.

00:22:36.560 --> 00:22:41.060
I think it could belong in games that are meant to be stressful races against the clock.

00:22:41.060 --> 00:22:46.320
But this game already has plenty of other things to do and things to worry about and stuff.

00:22:46.480 --> 00:22:53.100
It was weird to me to then have health and then also make it a race against the clock when you already have gold.

00:22:53.220 --> 00:22:54.160
Like, it just felt like...

00:22:54.160 --> 00:22:58.300
And it felt like they played the game and thought, eh, it's not difficult enough.

00:22:59.060 --> 00:23:03.320
You know, an easy way to make it harder is just to make you lose health automatically no matter what.

00:23:03.380 --> 00:23:04.620
And you have to constantly manage it.

00:23:04.620 --> 00:23:08.500
And it just didn't feel like it was, I don't know, integral to the gameplay.

00:23:09.280 --> 00:23:16.760
Yeah, to me, this health system is at odds with what feels natural to play the game.

00:23:17.000 --> 00:23:18.800
So a natural way to play the game.

00:23:19.020 --> 00:23:27.320
So because there's this, you know, this pressure to not have your health be completely drained,

00:23:27.580 --> 00:23:30.900
to me that seems like you'd want to get to the end of the level as soon as possible.

00:23:31.680 --> 00:23:34.380
Whereas that's not actually how you're supposed to play this game.

00:23:34.860 --> 00:23:42.480
You're supposed to keep, you know, keep replenishing your health over and over again by bombing out these large areas.

00:23:42.640 --> 00:23:49.360
But that doesn't seem in line with what it's, like, what it appears to be off the bat.

00:23:49.600 --> 00:23:51.140
So that, I don't know. Totally.

00:23:51.280 --> 00:23:55.260
No, I get you, Sam, because the game is at odds with itself in a lot of situations.

00:23:55.260 --> 00:24:01.860
You know, we're talking about, like, it wants you to explore, but it doesn't necessarily, like, reward exploration in the best possible manner.

00:24:01.920 --> 00:24:05.980
Because pickups are seemingly random depending on where you bomb.

00:24:06.080 --> 00:24:09.400
For the most part, I know, like, certain things are locked behind certain parts.

00:24:09.560 --> 00:24:14.600
But, like, some power-ups just won't appear in scenarios that they will for others.

00:24:14.600 --> 00:24:26.860
And some things that are, like, trap doors or entryways to another area aren't, like, they don't look like they have, like, a brittle section that you can bomb off.

00:24:26.960 --> 00:24:28.620
They just, you just have to know that they're there.

00:24:28.640 --> 00:24:31.340
So it, like, encourages that exploration, but then doesn't.

00:24:31.440 --> 00:24:33.100
Same thing with the health that you were talking about.

00:24:33.240 --> 00:24:38.300
Like, it wants you to explore, but doesn't give you the time to do so without constantly managing that health.

00:24:38.940 --> 00:24:40.640
So it is at odds with itself.

00:24:40.740 --> 00:24:44.800
But there's another thing there, Sam, that you talked about way early on in this episode.

00:24:44.960 --> 00:24:46.380
That it just, the controls.

00:24:46.660 --> 00:24:47.660
And it just feels good.

00:24:47.800 --> 00:24:53.100
And I think that now we're at a situation where we played almost 150 games.

00:24:53.300 --> 00:24:55.440
Well, 150th episode is next week.

00:24:56.380 --> 00:25:03.040
And we just kind of have, like, this, there's these tiers, right, to the controls in NES games where you just kind of, like, start up the game.

00:25:03.040 --> 00:25:10.600
And I think you know whether you're playing, like, a game that was well-programmed or not based on how it feels to be those characters.

00:25:10.620 --> 00:25:13.040
And I don't, I don't want to speak for everybody here.

00:25:13.140 --> 00:25:25.600
But this was a game that, like, upon boot up and seeing, like, the graphics and the way that Zed moved and the way that, like, the enemies interacted.

00:25:25.600 --> 00:25:28.200
Like, it is a tight game.

00:25:28.400 --> 00:25:29.340
Like, it is. Yeah, for sure.

00:25:29.480 --> 00:25:30.540
It is designed.

00:25:30.740 --> 00:25:33.780
And it is, and it does feel good to be Zed.

00:25:34.000 --> 00:25:39.980
So there is something there as a compliment that we haven't brought up yet of, like, just that, that instinctive knowledge.

00:25:40.000 --> 00:25:46.680
And maybe we can talk about that more of just, like, you have, like, a gut reaction to when you start up these NES games of what you're getting into, right?

00:25:47.080 --> 00:25:51.960
Well, I think that we're getting, like, we've almost, now we're almost getting a little spoiled with it.

00:25:52.660 --> 00:25:53.960
Maybe that's not the right way to phrase it.

00:25:54.060 --> 00:26:01.840
But, like, when we think back on, like, you know, when we first played Super Mario Brothers, obviously we had played it before.

00:26:01.860 --> 00:26:07.840
But in the context of all the games we were playing around Super Mario Brothers, we were like, oh, now this feels like a good video game.

00:26:07.860 --> 00:26:08.960
And we got a couple more of those.

00:26:09.060 --> 00:26:10.740
And usually they were good games.

00:26:10.840 --> 00:26:15.560
But I think now so many more are starting to look and feel really good.

00:26:15.560 --> 00:26:22.500
I mean, some of these levels in this game were giving me, like, Chrono Trigger vibes, which is obviously a very beautiful game on the Super Nintendo.

00:26:22.700 --> 00:26:26.300
Obviously it looks way better than this, but it was, like, it felt like we were going in that direction.

00:26:27.080 --> 00:26:34.280
But I think now there are so many games that are kind of getting it more with the feel of it and the look of it being, like, aesthetically pleasing and to feel good to play,

00:26:34.420 --> 00:26:43.080
that now we're going to get some games that look and feel good and maybe we don't like as much because there's just so many more people are able to do that.

00:26:43.080 --> 00:26:46.060
And maybe that's an opinion that's in the minority.

00:26:46.280 --> 00:26:52.460
I know you mentioned this was a hidden gem to some people, so maybe, you know, maybe there's more to this game that we're not seeing.

00:26:52.820 --> 00:26:55.680
Yeah, I'd say it's a very polished game.

00:26:56.860 --> 00:27:03.840
But, like, but, you know, it still has its issues as a whole game.

00:27:04.900 --> 00:27:07.220
But the presentation of it is very polished.

00:27:07.580 --> 00:27:21.220
And I think there's things that we would have mentioned in the past that, like, they would have gotten whole sections in our podcast, you know, power-ups, bosses, you know, the actual layout of the levels and things like that.

00:27:21.300 --> 00:27:23.340
Like, we would have spent time breaking those down.

00:27:23.520 --> 00:27:26.960
And I think we've done that enough now that we kind of don't have to do that for each game.

00:27:26.960 --> 00:27:30.340
We just kind of talk about, like, highlights of these particular games.

00:27:30.600 --> 00:27:36.640
But it's important to note, like, this game is like a, you know, it's no slog.

00:27:36.860 --> 00:27:39.020
It's, I think it's 27 levels.

00:27:39.880 --> 00:27:42.820
And there's, there are boss fights.

00:27:43.040 --> 00:27:45.980
It takes a little bit to get to those boss fights, but there are boss fights.

00:27:46.580 --> 00:27:48.000
There are unique levels.

00:27:48.180 --> 00:27:49.680
There's, like, there's a water level.

00:27:50.060 --> 00:27:52.020
There's an underground level.

00:27:52.240 --> 00:27:56.020
Like, there is, we used to reward that, right, of, like, feeling like you're going on a journey.

00:27:56.020 --> 00:28:01.180
And we're kind of passing that by here in this episode.

00:28:01.180 --> 00:28:08.420
So I just wonder if for you guys, like, were you surprised that these things were in the game on top of everything else that's here?

00:28:08.560 --> 00:28:14.380
Like, or was it just expected now that we're, like, moving in throughout the NES catalog?

00:28:15.220 --> 00:28:23.860
I'd say that it's become less of a pleasant surprise when games are as feature complete as this one is.

00:28:24.880 --> 00:28:27.080
It used to just be a breath of fresh air.

00:28:27.680 --> 00:28:40.480
And, like, oh, thank God I'm playing a game that seems like it was crafted instead of just, like, it's, like, the most basic interactive medium that we can think of.

00:28:40.480 --> 00:28:51.000
So, yeah, we're definitely no longer as kind just because it reaches, like, this bar of quality.

00:28:51.280 --> 00:28:54.560
Because I do think that this is a quality game.

00:28:55.420 --> 00:29:06.140
Like, no matter what problems we have with, like, the more macro gameplay loop, like, it's well designed in some respects.

00:29:07.240 --> 00:29:08.720
But, no, you're right.

00:29:08.860 --> 00:29:16.560
Like, we don't, this isn't going to automatically become our favorite game just because it hits those bars now.

00:29:45.080 --> 00:29:46.480
We'll see you next time.

00:30:16.820 --> 00:30:30.900
And if we can just talk about power-ups since they are a big part of this game in a way that, like, you don't necessarily need, as far as I understand, you don't need power-ups for any particular situation.

00:30:30.900 --> 00:30:36.500
It's not like Metroid where you're, like, locked behind something until you get that specific power-up.

00:30:36.500 --> 00:30:39.420
But there's a lot of different kinds of power-ups to collect.

00:30:40.380 --> 00:30:47.260
And there's, like, a, it's an interesting way of handling it because there are so many that you have to go into your menu and select them.

00:30:47.340 --> 00:30:49.360
And then that's how you'll be able to use them.

00:30:49.900 --> 00:30:52.760
I'm fine with that when there's this many options.

00:30:52.980 --> 00:30:56.340
I'm wondering, did any of these power-ups stand out to you guys?

00:30:56.400 --> 00:31:00.100
Like, was there anything that you were like, oh, that's a really cool thing that we haven't seen yet?

00:31:00.100 --> 00:31:23.420
I mean, not that we haven't seen yet, but, like, the missile that'll clean out, like, an entire row of destructible objects felt really good just because we've gotten so used to, like, just by playing the game with the bombs that can do, like, one on each side.

00:31:24.260 --> 00:31:29.160
But just because we have that knowledge, it feels really good to just clear out an entire line.

00:31:30.380 --> 00:31:31.920
But, like, that's not something new.

00:31:32.080 --> 00:31:33.340
But it did feel good.

00:31:33.620 --> 00:31:35.040
Right. That was my favorite, too.

00:31:35.100 --> 00:31:36.180
And that's a good point, actually.

00:31:36.380 --> 00:31:44.560
I mean, they designed it very well to feel very satisfying because the bombs, you got used to the much less satisfying bombs.

00:31:45.560 --> 00:31:52.240
But I do think that there were even some power-ups that you do kind of need if you want to play the game naturally, like the candles.

00:31:52.640 --> 00:31:54.860
I mean, technically, you can get through it without the candles.

00:31:55.020 --> 00:32:01.580
But, like, if you're genuinely a beginner at this game and you genuinely want to try and play it, you sort of need the candles.

00:32:02.280 --> 00:32:06.980
Oh, yeah. It's like going through those cave levels in Pokemon without Flash, right?

00:32:07.060 --> 00:32:08.940
Right, right. You have to really know what you're doing.

00:32:09.160 --> 00:32:13.620
I think that was easier because maybe I just had a lot more time on my hands when I was playing Pokemon.

00:32:13.820 --> 00:32:15.540
But I used to be able to do that.

00:32:15.700 --> 00:32:18.560
This, I just feel like, would not even be enjoyable to attempt.

00:32:20.140 --> 00:32:25.880
Correct me if I'm wrong, but isn't there another level later on that is dark, completely dark also, and you need another?

00:32:26.520 --> 00:32:30.280
You need to have collected something else to just light it up, and it just lights it up permanently.

00:32:30.520 --> 00:32:33.800
I think that's the third level.

00:32:34.100 --> 00:32:35.120
The lamp, right?

00:32:35.320 --> 00:32:39.080
Yeah. Because that felt weird as if it was a Metroidvania type thing.

00:32:40.460 --> 00:32:44.540
But it's so linear that it doesn't really, it's weird that it's like, oh, you could have just walked by it.

00:32:44.600 --> 00:32:45.440
Too late. You don't have it.

00:32:45.660 --> 00:32:46.700
You're in a dark level now.

00:32:47.780 --> 00:32:49.060
Yeah, that was a goofy decision.

00:32:49.600 --> 00:32:57.500
A lot of these power-ups, though, they feel, like, shmup-inspired, you know, for better or for worse.

00:32:57.520 --> 00:32:58.400
I think that's really cool.

00:32:58.400 --> 00:33:04.920
Like, the flash one that just automatically destroys all enemies on screen, I feel like we saw that in games like Zanac.

00:33:06.160 --> 00:33:09.500
And the crossfire one that lets you shoot in all four directions.

00:33:10.420 --> 00:33:17.200
Another thing that just feels like something that would be more of, like, a power-up to your ship than a power-up to your robot cyborg.

00:33:17.200 --> 00:33:28.880
Yeah. So it's sort of like, we're getting the good stuff from shmups, but we're also getting sort of the bad stuff that we've seen in other adventure-ish games.

00:33:29.720 --> 00:33:39.220
Where the, well, what it's taking from these adventure-ish games are these upgrades that are really just key items.

00:33:39.500 --> 00:33:43.740
Like, the lantern serves, it doesn't make you feel powerful.

00:33:43.740 --> 00:33:45.760
It doesn't, like, add anything to the gameplay.

00:33:45.760 --> 00:33:50.660
It's just basically a key item so that you're not playing a level in the dark.

00:33:51.400 --> 00:33:58.560
But it's also taking a bunch of these shmup power-ups that actually add something to the gameplay.

00:33:58.700 --> 00:33:59.560
Like, they're situational.

00:33:59.800 --> 00:34:03.140
Like, you're not going to want to waste all your missiles just because they're the most powerful,

00:34:03.180 --> 00:34:07.740
because there may just be a spot where you want to clear out an entire line.

00:34:07.740 --> 00:34:18.720
Or you find yourself sort of cornered, and you might want that omnidirectional shot that you wouldn't just want to have on at all times.

00:34:19.360 --> 00:34:24.120
So I like that they took that stuff from the shmups.

00:34:24.120 --> 00:34:30.540
I could have gone without the glorified key items.

00:34:31.720 --> 00:34:35.180
But I think it was a good balance, at least, if they're going to do one or the other.

00:34:35.660 --> 00:34:39.220
My favorite power-up was the boots that make you go a little bit faster.

00:34:39.660 --> 00:34:40.940
Just a little bit faster.

00:34:41.520 --> 00:34:42.920
It's, like, almost hard to notice.

00:34:43.580 --> 00:34:45.000
And, you know, what else?

00:34:45.180 --> 00:34:47.520
I mean, like, the music was great.

00:34:47.660 --> 00:34:54.540
Yeah. And I really hated when your health is low enough that the music just goes away and you just get this annoying beeping sound instead.

00:34:55.000 --> 00:34:56.140
That's the worst. That was awful.

00:34:56.200 --> 00:35:00.060
It was the worst. Yeah, it's not even, like, a video game beeping sound.

00:35:00.200 --> 00:35:02.200
It's like an alarm clock.

00:35:02.360 --> 00:35:04.180
Yeah. Like a digital alarm clock beeping sound.

00:35:05.000 --> 00:35:08.640
I actually had, I feel like I had a spike of adrenaline when that happened.

00:35:08.640 --> 00:35:17.600
Like, the same, like, just, oh my god, everything hurts of, like, when you are, like, you snoozed and now you're late.

00:35:18.120 --> 00:35:20.660
